From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: reset the write queue and DSP buffer index on prepare

After any stop/start of the same PCM (mpv seek or loop, snd_pcm_drop +
prepare, xrun recovery) playback never advanced again: either nothing was
queued, or "Error queuing playback buffer -16" repeated until close.

snd_pcm_prepare() restarts the stream at frame 0 (snd_pcm_post_prepare()
sets appl_ptr = hw_ptr = 0), but q6asm_dai_prepare() kept prtd->queue_ptr
from the previous run. In .ack, appl_ptr - queue_ptr then wraps
(unsigned) and the int period count is garbage: when negative nothing is
queued and the stream stalls; when positive WRITE_V2 packets are sent
until GLINK has no free intents and rpmsg_trysend() returns -EBUSY, on
every later ack too.

q6asm.c had the same stale state one layer down: the port's dsp_buf
(next buffer index to write) and hw_ptr (last completed period) survived
the unmap/remap that every re-prepare does, so the first write after a
restart came from the wrong period and the pointer reported the previous
run's position.

Reset queue_ptr in prepare, and dsp_buf/hw_ptr when a new buffer table
is mapped. Also keep queue_ptr in appl_ptr's boundary range and report
an xrun instead of flooding the DSP if appl_ptr ever falls behind it.
Pause/resume (CMD_PAUSE / RUN) was not affected.

Tested on the ROG Phone 5 (SM8350): hw:0,0 drop+prepare+restart x8 with
pause/resume after each, mpv audio-only with --loop-file and IPC seeks,
mpv 1080p video with seeks/pause; hw_ptr advances every time, no -EBUSY.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c	2026-09-26 13:26:25.297576098 +0200
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c	2026-09-26 13:27:04.014863968 +0200
@@ -243,6 +243,16 @@
 		prtd->state = Q6ASM_STREAM_STOPPED;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The core restarts the stream at frame 0: snd_pcm_post_prepare() sets
+	 * appl_ptr = hw_ptr = 0 after this callback. A queue_ptr left over from
+	 * the previous run (stop/drop, xrun, seek) is then ahead of appl_ptr,
+	 * .ack computes a bogus period count and either queues nothing or floods
+	 * the DSP until the APR/GLINK queue is full (-EBUSY); the stream never
+	 * advances again.
+	 */
+	prtd->queue_ptr = 0;
+
 	ret = q6asm_map_memory_regions(substream->stream, prtd->audio_client,
 				       prtd->phys,
 				       (prtd->pcm_size / prtd->periods),
@@ -313,10 +323,30 @@
 {
 	struct snd_pcm_runtime *runtime = substream->runtime;
 	struct q6asm_dai_rtd *prtd = runtime->private_data;
+	snd_pcm_uframes_t appl_ptr, pending;
 	int i, ret = 0, avail_periods;
 
 	if (substream->stream == SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_PLAYBACK && prtd->state == Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING) {
-		avail_periods = (runtime->control->appl_ptr - prtd->queue_ptr)/runtime->period_size;
+		/* appl_ptr wraps at the boundary; keep queue_ptr in the same range */
+		appl_ptr = READ_ONCE(runtime->control->appl_ptr);
+		if (appl_ptr >= prtd->queue_ptr)
+			pending = appl_ptr - prtd->queue_ptr;
+		else
+			pending = runtime->boundary - prtd->queue_ptr + appl_ptr;
+
+		/*
+		 * More than a buffer ahead means appl_ptr moved back without a
+		 * prepare (e.g. SNDRV_PCM_IOCTL_RESET while running). Report an
+		 * xrun so the application re-prepares instead of queuing garbage.
+		 */
+		if (pending > runtime->buffer_size) {
+			dev_err_ratelimited(component->dev,
+					    "playback queue out of sync (appl %lu queued %lu)\n",
+					    appl_ptr, prtd->queue_ptr);
+			return -EPIPE;
+		}
+
+		avail_periods = pending / runtime->period_size;
 		for (i = 0; i < avail_periods; i++) {
 			ret = q6asm_write_async(prtd->audio_client, prtd->stream_id,
 					   prtd->pcm_count, 0, 0, 0);
@@ -326,6 +356,8 @@
 				return ret;
 			}
 			prtd->queue_ptr += runtime->period_size;
+			if (prtd->queue_ptr >= runtime->boundary)
+				prtd->queue_ptr -= runtime->boundary;
 		}
 	}
 
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c	2026-09-26 13:26:25.297474657 +0200
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm.c	2026-09-26 13:26:42.198827995 +0200
@@ -525,6 +525,15 @@
 		}
 	}
 	ac->port[dir].num_periods = periods;
+	/*
+	 * A new mapping starts a new stream (every q6asm-dai prepare remaps):
+	 * the first buffer the client fills is period 0 and no period has
+	 * completed yet. Without this, a stream restarted after stop/drop sent
+	 * its first write from where the previous run left off and reported
+	 * that run's hardware pointer.
+	 */
+	ac->port[dir].dsp_buf = 0;
+	atomic_set(&ac->port[dir].hw_ptr, 0);
 
 	spin_unlock_irqrestore(&ac->lock, flags);
 
